===Adjective===
{{head|en|adjective}}

# Of or relating to the biological theory of [[evolution]].
#* {{quote-journal|lang=en|date=2013-03
|author=[[w:Harold J. Morowitz|Harold J. Morowitz]]
|title=The Smallest Cell
|volume=101|issue=2|page=83
|magazine=[[w:American Scientist|American Scientist]]
|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/2/the-smallest-cell
|passage=It is likely that the long '''evolutionary''' trajectory of ''Mycoplasma'' went from a reductive autotroph to oxidative heterotroph to a cell-wall–defective degenerate parasite. This '''evolutionary''' trajectory assumes the simplicity to complexity route of biogenesis, a point of view that is not universally accepted.}}
#: ''The '''evolutionary''' history of marine mammals includes land-dwelling ancestors.''
# Having formal similarities to the biological theory of evolution.
#* {{quote-journal|lang=en|month=Dec.|year=1974|volume=84|issue=336|pages=886&ndash;905
|title=Neoclassical vs. '''Evolutionary''' Theories of Economic Growth: Critique and Prospectus
|author1-first=Richard R.|author1-last=Nelson
|author2-first=Sidney G.|author2-last=Winter
|work=The Economic Journal
|doi=10.2307/2230572|jstor=2230572
|passage=The basic elements of an '''evolutionary''' growth theory are discussed in Section II.}}

